        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दाल",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दाल (dāl) — \"lentils, split pulses\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit दल् (dal-), 'to split', through the noun दल (dala), 'a piece torn off'. दाल (dāl) is not the name of a plant at all — it is the name of what was done to the seed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Whole pulses are not दाल (dāl); split ones are. So the word draws its line through the middle of the lentil rather than around the outside of the species, which is why one plant can give both a दाल (dāl) and a not-दाल (dāl)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The second of five, and the one named after a knife rather than a plant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
