              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सब्ज़ी (sabzī) — \"a vegetable, vegetables\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A Persian word: sabz means 'green', and -ī turns an adjective into a noun. सब्ज़ी (sabzī) is 'greenery' — the green things, taken together."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have met this suffix already without being told: ख़ुशी (khushī), 'happiness', is khush, 'pleased', with the same -ī on the end. One ending, two words, both Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
